  "dct_description_sm": [
    "Contained within the 4th Edition (1974) of the Atlas of Canada is a map that shows the area of wetlands as a percentage of grid-units, 10 000 square kilometres in area. The term, wetlands, as used on this map, refers to areas represented on the 1:250 000 scale maps of the National Topographical System. These areas include inundated lands (seasonal), marsh or swamp, alkali flats, string bog and foreshore flats."
